        <div class="ons-text-container">
          <p>Figure 2 shows the contributions from the 12 divisions to the change in the annual Consumer Prices Index including owner occupiers' housing costs (CPIH) inflation rate between July and August 2026. These sum to the change in the annual rate, from 3.1% to 3.3%, between these months.</p>
          <p>The increase in the 12-month rate between July and August 2026 reflected upward contributions from six divisions, partially offset by downward contributions from two divisions. The largest upward contribution came from transport, particularly motor fuels. There were no large, offsetting downward contributions.</p>
          <h3>Transport</h3>
          <p>Prices in the transport division rose overall by 4.6% in the 12 months to August 2026, up from 3.6% the previous month (Figure 3). On a monthly basis, prices rose by 1.5% in August 2026, compared with a rise of 0.4% a year ago.</p>
        </div>

