        <div class="ons-text-container">
          <p>The largest upward effect contributing to the rise in the transport annual rate came from motor fuels.</p>
          <p>The average price of petrol rose by 9.1 pence per litre between July and August 2026, compared with a rise of 0.3 pence per litre between July and August 2025. The average price stood at 161.3 pence per litre in August 2026. This is the highest price recorded since November 2022. Diesel prices rose by 14.2 pence per litre in August 2026, compared with a rise of 0.8 pence per litre in August 2025. The average price stood at 181.8 pence per litre in August 2026.</p>
          <p>These movements resulted in overall motor fuel prices rising by 23.0% in the 12 months to August 2026, compared with a rise of 15.5% the previous month.</p>
          <p>Within transport, there was a much smaller upward effect from air fares, and partially offsetting small downward effects from vehicle maintenance and repair, and rail fares.</p>
          <p>Air fares rose by 6.2% between July and August 2026, compared with a rise of 2.1% between July and August 2025. The upward effect came from long-haul routes where fares rose in August 2026, compared with a fall a year ago.</p>
          <p>All domestic and European flight prices were collected after the outbreak of the conflict in the Middle East on 28 February 2026. Long-haul flight prices collected three months and one month before departure were also collected after the outbreak of the conflict, but prices collected six months before departure were collected before the outbreak.</p>
          <p>Prices for vehicle maintenance and repair fell this year by more than a year ago, with the downward effect coming from roadside recovery services. Overall rail fares fell this year, compared with a rise a year ago, with the effect coming from international rail travel.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ons-text-container">
          <h3>Food and alcoholic beverages</h3>
          <p>The 12-month inflation rate for food and non-alcoholic beverages was 1.3% in August 2026, unchanged from July (Figure 4). The rate was last lower in September 2021, when it was 0.8%. On a monthly basis, food and non-alcoholic beverage prices rose by 0.4% in August 2026, the same rise as in August 2025.</p>
